<title>SINGAPORE: Hwa Hong 1st-half net slips 2.15 pct.</title>
<headline>Hwa Hong 1st-half net slips 2.15 pct.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1996-09-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to June 30, 1996</p>
<p>		   (in millions of S$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit			    7.91   vs   8.09</p>
<p>    Profit per share (cents)	  5.41   vs   5.53</p>
<p>    Turnover			    209.71   vs 111.67</p>
<p>    Investment income		   0.56   vs   0.35</p>
<p>    Other income incl interest	3.37   vs   3.23</p>
<p>    Interest (expense)		  0.27   vs   0.46</p>
<p>    Depreciation/amortization	 1.02   vs   1.20</p>
<p>    Income from associates	    3.30   vs   2.45</p>
<p>    Pre-tax profit			9.63   vs  10.28</p>
<p>    Tax				     1.71   vs   2.18</p>
<p>Note - Hwa Hong Corp Ltd has interests in insurance, warehouse rentals, packaging of edible oil products, trading in consumer products and piling and construction.</p>
<p>It said the lower profit was due to a provision of Singapore $1.9 million for a completed project under dispute and an increase in reserves for unexpired risks in insurance premiums.</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom (65 8703080)</p>
</text>
